  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crisis Medical Response for Lebanon - AUB</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Lebanon):  Through the Crisis Medical Response (CMR Lebanon) activity, which was awarded in January 2024 using Complex Crises Funds, USAID has supported the American University of Beirut Medical Center (AUBMC), to pre-position medical supplies and equipment and prepare their workforce to respond successfully to mass casualty incidents. To leverage and complement these prior investments and given the dire economic context facing Lebanon and recent fighting between Hizballah and Israel that has led to even more significant economic losses, university hospitals are now struggling to cope with high costs and high volatility of availability of diesel fuel for generators due to lack of reliable grid-provided electricity. As such, FY24 assistance will support the AUBMC in purchasing American-made solar panels to promote energy independence and long-term sustainable solutions, cut costs, and save critical resources. This $5M meets the $5M directive in the 653a report for hospital energy programs.</narrative>
  </description>
